# Build output. Anything starting with "build" -- build/, build-win/, and any
# other tree someone points cmake at -- so a stray -B directory cannot be
# committed by a careless `git add -A`, which is exactly how a 5 MB Windows DLL
# once got in here.
/build*/
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
Makefile

# Python bytecode from tools/analysis
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Local reference material: recordings and screenshots supplied for comparison
# while working on the plugin. Not part of the project, and not ours to ship.
# The leading "!" has to be escaped or git reads it as a negation.
/\!dev/

# Editor and OS noise
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
